---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Studio — SlushTec"
  description="About SlushTec: Tucson indie studio building adult interactive worlds with permanent residual. VARP engine, True Emotion Engine, original-IP World Packs. Fail-forward, local-first."
  image="/images/hero-residual.jpg"
>
  <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-12 pt-14 sm:pt-20 pb-12">
    <p class="text-warm-earth text-sm font-medium tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">
      Tucson, Arizona
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight mb-6">Studio</h1>
    <div class="score-line max-w-sm mb-12"></div>

    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 lg:gap-16">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-6 text-gray-300 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          SlushTec builds adult interactive worlds where free-form action writes durable state,
          relationships are bidirectional, and the world keeps score. Not chatbots with furniture —
          living reactive spaces.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our core systems are the <strong class="text-white">VARP</strong> engine
          (Virtual Action Role Play) and the <strong class="text-white">True Emotion Engine</strong>.
          NPCs form bias and residue the way people do, not as forgetful transcripts.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every design choice bends toward the illusion of free will inside pack-local social residual —
          crush, jealousy, stew, confront — without building a full simulated mind.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-surface bg-surface/30 p-7 sm:p-8">
          <p class="text-sm tracking-[0.15em] uppercase text-golden-glow mb-5">Hard lines</p>
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-base text-gray-300">
            <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-warm-earth">▸</span> Permanent score / fail-forward</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-warm-earth">▸</span> Local-first residual ownership</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-warm-earth">▸</span> Adult 18+ only</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-warm-earth">▸</span> No minors / CSAM — absolute</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-warm-earth">▸</span> Original IP World Packs</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-warm-earth">▸</span> Worlds, not agendas</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Differentiation -->
  <section class="border-t border-surface bg-surface/25">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-12 py-16 sm:py-20">
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-semibold text-golden-glow mb-10 tracking-tight">What sets us apart</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-base text-left border-collapse min-w-[560px]">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-surface text-gray-500">
              <th class="py-4 pr-8 font-medium w-1/2">Others often ship</th>
              <th class="py-4 font-medium text-golden-glow">SlushTec ships</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-gray-300">
            <tr class="border-b border-surface/50"><td class="py-4 pr-8">Chat with a character</td><td class="py-4"><strong class="text-white">Act</strong> inside a reactive mini-universe</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-surface/50"><td class="py-4 pr-8">Soft reset / reload the bad choice</td><td class="py-4"><strong class="text-white">Permanent ledger</strong> — fail forward, no paid undo</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-surface/50"><td class="py-4 pr-8">One-way affection that only climbs</td><td class="py-4"><strong class="text-white">Bidirectional</strong> trust and intimacy that can collapse</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-surface/50"><td class="py-4 pr-8">Generic helpful NPC voice</td><td class="py-4"><strong class="text-white">World-pack authenticity</strong> — realm rules, not customer service</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-surface/50"><td class="py-4 pr-8">Scripted trees or forgetful sessions</td><td class="py-4"><strong class="text-white">VARP + True Emotion Engine</strong> — bias, residue, durable state</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-surface/50"><td class="py-4 pr-8">Cloud-only dependency</td><td class="py-4"><strong class="text-white">Local-first</strong> (optional cloud for art / Avatar Lab)</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="py-4 pr-8">Franchise skin over a chatbot</td><td class="py-4"><strong class="text-white">Original IP</strong> world packs on a shared engine</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lineage -->
  <section class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-12 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-semibold text-golden-glow mb-6 tracking-tight">The VARP lineage</h2>
    <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-gray-300 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Live Action Role Play asked for decades whether you could step into the story instead of only describing it.
        Persistent digital worlds proved people would treat a place as a second life.
        Language models finally supplied reactive agents. What almost nobody did was put the pieces back together:
        free-form action + permanent score + world law + agents that form bias instead of forgetting.
      </p>
      <p>
        VARP is that line. The chat window was a detour — not the destination.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-500 mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-surface max-w-3xl">
      Founded by Brian “Slush” Slusher. Studio name and domain locked 2026.
      Built under a hard sun.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
